From: mozixun <mozixun@fedoraproject.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: handle a null device in the RAW plugin

QImageReader::supportedImageFormats() calls capabilities() with a null
device.  The plugin dereferenced it, which crashes every Qt application
that enumerates image formats, including Treeland.

--- a/qimage-plugins/libraw/main.cpp
+++ b/qimage-plugins/libraw/main.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@
 FreeimageQt5Plugin::capabilities(QIODevice *device, const QByteArray &format) const
 {
     Capabilities cap;
+    if (!device)
+        return cap;
+
     if (keys().contains(format.toUpper()) ||
             format == "tif" ||
             format == "tiff") {
